<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">quality</ansi>

Quality is workmanship, and it is separate from rarity: an exquisite common
sword is possible. Quality changes a weapon's damage bonus and an armor's
protection, and what the item is worth. It is part of the item's name:
"fine short sword". A standard item has no quality word.

  Quality     Base stats   Worth     Chance
  crude         -20%        x0.4      10%
  worn          -10%        x0.7      20%
  standard      as made     x1        45%
  fine          +10%        x1.6      17%
  superior      +20%        x2.5       7%
  exquisite     +30%        x4         1%

The percentage applies to the base type's damage and protection, rounded,
and always moves a weapon or armor by at least 1 either way, so a fine
dagger is a little better than a standard one.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help rarity</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help itemlevel</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help affixes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help equipment</ansi>.
